#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`out_flags:\\n  separate_out: true`"
msgstr "`out_flags:\\n  separate_out: true`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:199
msgid ""
"An **independent field**, not half of a group: a source setting this one "
"leaves [`compressed`](#compressed) to whatever another source said."
msgstr ""
"Un **campo indipendente**, non la metà di un gruppo: una sorgente che "
"imposti questo lascia [`compressed`](#compressed) a quanto ha detto "
"un'altra sorgente."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:205
msgid "`compressed`"
msgstr "`compressed`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--archive`, `-z` — present means true, absent means *nothing said*"
msgstr "`--archive`, `-z` — presente significa vero, assente significa *non detto*"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`FREEPORTS_ARCHIVE` — same boolean grammar"
msgstr "`FREEPORTS_ARCHIVE` — stessa grammatica booleana"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`out_flags.archive` — a real YAML boolean"
msgstr "`out_flags.archive` — un vero booleano YAML"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`FREEPORTS_ARCHIVE=false`"
msgstr "`FREEPORTS_ARCHIVE=false`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:218
msgid ""
"Publicly the option is called **archive**, on every source. `compressed` "
"is only its internal field name, and `out_flags: compressed:` in a file "
"is rejected as an unknown sub-key."
msgstr ""
"Pubblicamente l'opzione si chiama **archive**, su ogni sorgente. "
"`compressed` è solo il suo nome interno di campo, e `out_flags: "
"compressed:` in un file è rifiutata come sottochiave sconosciuta."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:221
msgid "Also switched on implicitly by an `out_path` ending in `.tar.gz`."
msgstr "Accesa implicitamente anche da un `out_path` che finisca in `.tar.gz`."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--no-download` — present sets it **false**; absent means *nothing said*"
msgstr ""
"`--no-download` — presente la imposta a **falso**; assente significa *non"
" detto*"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`FREEPORTS_SAVE_PDF` — the boolean grammar"
msgstr "`FREEPORTS_SAVE_PDF` — la grammatica booleana"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`save_pdf` — a real YAML boolean"
msgstr "`save_pdf` — un vero booleano YAML"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`save pdf` — literally `true` or `false`"
msgstr "`save pdf` — letteralmente `true` oppure `false`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`true`"
msgstr "`true`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "the boolean grammar; then it changes how document paths are validated"
msgstr ""
"la grammatica booleana; poi cambia il modo in cui si validano i percorsi "
"dei documenti"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--no-download`, `save_pdf: false`"
msgstr "`--no-download`, `save_pdf: false`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:239
msgid ""
"The one option whose command-line spelling is negative, which is why the "
"flag's name misleads: `--no-download` does not suppress the download, it "
"suppresses **keeping** the downloaded file."
msgstr ""
"L'unica impostazione la cui grafia sulla riga di comando è negativa, ed è"
" il motivo per cui il nome del flag inganna: `--no-download` non "
"impedisce lo scaricamento, impedisce di **conservare** il file scaricato."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--workers`, `-j`"
msgstr "`--workers`, `-j`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "a positive integer, or `auto`"
msgstr "un intero positivo, oppure `auto`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`auto`"
msgstr "`auto`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "zero and negatives are a typed error naming the option"
msgstr "zero e i negativi sono un errore tipizzato che nomina l'opzione"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`-j 4`, `n_workers: auto`"
msgstr "`-j 4`, `n_workers: auto`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:258
msgid ""
"The **global default of both levels**, not a process count. It is what "
"gives `-j 1` a universal meaning: one job at a time *and* one page at a "
"time. A level with its own value ignores it."
msgstr ""
"Il **valore predefinito globale di entrambi i livelli**, non un conteggio"
" di processi. È ciò che dà a `-j 1` un significato universale: un job per"
" volta *e* una pagina per volta. Un livello con un valore proprio lo "
"ignora."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:264
msgid "`parallelism_jobs`"
msgstr "`parallelism_jobs`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--jobs` — long form only, `-j` being taken by the global default"
msgstr ""
"`--jobs` — solo forma lunga, dato che `-j` è preso dal valore predefinito"
" globale"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "unset — inherits `n_workers`"
msgstr "non impostato — eredita da `n_workers`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "as `n_workers`, with this option's name in the error"
msgstr "come `n_workers`, con il nome di questa opzione nell'errore"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--jobs 2`"
msgstr "`--jobs 2`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:277
msgid ""
"Left unset on purpose by the defaults tier: a level nobody touched has no"
" value of its own and inherits the global one. Were the defaults to fill "
"it in, the global default could no longer reach it."
msgstr ""
"Lasciato non impostato apposta dal livello dei valori predefiniti: un "
"livello che nessuno ha toccato non ha un valore proprio ed eredita quello"
" globale. Se i valori predefiniti lo riempissero, il valore predefinito "
"globale non potrebbe più raggiungerlo."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:284
msgid "`parallelism_pages`"
msgstr "`parallelism_pages`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "as `n_workers`"
msgstr "come `n_workers`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`parallelism:\\n  pages: auto`"
msgstr "`parallelism:\\n  pages: auto`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--batch`, `-b`"
msgstr "`--batch`, `-b`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "none — not in batch mode"
msgstr "nessuno — non in modalità a lotti"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "the CSV is read and its columns checked; an unknown column is an error"
msgstr ""
"il CSV è letto e le sue colonne controllate; una colonna sconosciuta è un"
" errore"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`-b jobs.csv`"
msgstr "`-b jobs.csv`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:313
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{doc}`../../guides/user/advanced/batch`."
msgstr "{doc}`../../guides/user/advanced/batch`."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:318
msgid "`config_file`"
msgstr "`config_file`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "none — the three tiers are searched instead"
msgstr "nessuno — si cercano invece i tre livelli"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "the file is parsed; unknown keys are errors"
msgstr "si fa il parsing del file; le chiavi sconosciute sono errori"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`--config ./ci-freeports.yaml`"
msgstr "`--config ./ci-freeports.yaml`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:331
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"No YAML spelling, for the obvious reason: a configuration file naming the"
" configuration file to read would be a chicken with no egg. "
"{doc}`config_file` lists the tiers searched when this is unset."
msgstr ""
"Nessuna grafia YAML, per il motivo ovvio: un file di configurazione che "
"nominasse il file di configurazione da leggere sarebbe una gallina senza "
"uovo. {doc}`config_file` elenca i livelli che si cercano quando questa "
"non è impostata."

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`-v` and `-q`, both **counted** and independent"
msgstr "`-v` e `-q`, entrambe **contate** e indipendenti"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`FREEPORTS_VERBOSITY` — by variant name, case-insensitively"
msgstr ""
"`FREEPORTS_VERBOSITY` — per nome della variante, senza distinzione fra "
"maiuscole e minuscole"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`verbosity` — same names"
msgstr "`verbosity` — stessi nomi"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "one of `silent`, `error`, `warn`, `info`, `debug`, `trace`"
msgstr "uno fra `silent`, `error`, `warn`, `info`, `debug`, `trace`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`warn`"
msgstr "`warn`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "the name; the counts are clamped and can never be out of range"
msgstr ""
"il nome; i conteggi sono riportati dentro i limiti e non possono mai "
"uscire dall'intervallo"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`-vv`, `FREEPORTS_VERBOSITY=trace`"
msgstr "`-vv`, `FREEPORTS_VERBOSITY=trace`"

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:351
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"All three forms are applied, but not at the same instant: `-v`/`-q` "
"govern from the first line logged, while the environment and YAML forms "
"take effect the moment the configuration resolves. See {doc}`index` for "
"the one consequence."
msgstr ""
"Tutte e tre le forme sono applicate, ma non nello stesso istante: "
"`-v`/`-q` governano dalla prima riga di log, mentre le forme d'ambiente e"
" YAML entrano in vigore nel momento in cui la configurazione si risolve. "
"Vedi {doc}`index` per l'unica conseguenza."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The environment and YAML forms are "
#~ "parsed, validated and merged but **do"
#~ " not reach the parent process's "
#~ "logging** — see {doc}`index`. Today only"
